     "text": "Nine pages published in 2008 changed global finance forever, because you think a massive corporate team built cryptocurrency, but an unknown person named Satoshi Nakamoto created it, publishing a whitepaper when the financial system broke down. You expect banks to control every dollar, but in 2009 Bitcoin launched as the world's first decentralized digital currency, operating without any central authority or government permission. Traditional money prints endlessly, so inflation destroys your savings over time, yet Bitcoin operates with a strict twenty-one million supply cap. Nine pages and a hard cap replaced the central bank."
